  "description": "Inspects Filestore capacity and utilization on Google Cloud, evaluates storage scaling rules, and performs capacity autoscaling (scale UP for low free space or scale DOWN for cost optimization). Use when monitoring Filestore instance headroom, resizing instance shares, configuring automated growth/shrink thresholds (custom thresholds apply globally across projects in session memory), or preventing out-of-space outages. Don't use for Cloud Storage (GCS) buckets, Persistent Disk block storage, or NetApp Volumes.",
